            trusting a3(0) (two DIFFERENT numerical methods each)
======================================================================

a2'(0) analytic (via psi1_prime)   = -519816.636488
a2'(0) central finite-difference   = -519816.636719  (h=1e-06)
  relative difference: 4.44e-10
  ODE-shooting b2(0) with s_far=0.1: -20785.081735
  ODE-shooting b2(0) with s_far=0.12: -20813.663904
  ODE-shooting b2(0) with s_far=0.15: -20816.594330
  ODE-shooting b2(0) with s_far=0.2: -20816.636483

Quadrature-based b2(0) (Part C, above): -20816.636488
(If shooting disagrees with the quadrature value as s_far grows, that
 signals the 'bounded at infinity' boundary condition is numerically
 delicate -- exp(c*s^2/2) blowup means shooting backward from a
 not-large-enough s_far is itself a poor approximation to the true
 s->infinity limit; the quadrature form is analytically exact for
 s_far->infinity and does not suffer this specific finite-cutoff
 bias, so it -- not the shooting value -- is treated as ground truth
 below, with the shooting run reported only as a rough sanity check.)

